---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import MethodologySection from '../components/MethodologySection.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="About"
  description="Elliott English and Mac Steele — operations leadership and a career of matching technology to real business problems, now building AI systems that target your real constraint."
>
  <section class="about-hero section-dark">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <p class="section-label">About</p>
      <h1 class="about-title">Operations leader turned AI builder.</h1>
      <p class="about-subtitle">
        20 years of finding where complex organizations are actually broken and fixing the system, not just the symptom.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-story section">
    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="photo-placeholder">
        <span>Photo</span>
      </div>
      <div class="story-content">
        <p class="section-label">The Thread</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">One career, one thread.</h2>
        <p>
          My career has been one long thread: finding where complex organizations are actually broken and fixing the system, not just the symptom. I've done it at a Pentagon desk in Qatar, running derivatives metrics and fraud operations at Morgan Stanley, inside a national pharma agency, and while building a telehealth division from scratch.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI is just the newest and most powerful tool I've brought to that same problem.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most AI consultants will sell you automation. I'll find out if automation is even the right move. My background is operations — Air Force, Morgan Stanley, healthcare systems. I've spent 20 years finding where businesses actually break. AI is the most powerful fix I've ever had access to, but only if you aim it at the right place.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <section class="about-difference section">
    <p class="section-label">Why This Is Different</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">What I bring that most AI consultants don't</h2>

    <div class="diff-grid">
      <div class="diff-card">
        <h3>Operational Analysis</h3>
        <p>I don't start with a list of AI tools. I start by mapping your entire value stream end-to-end, finding where work piles up, where customers wait, and where the real constraint lives.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diff-card">
        <h3>Theory of Constraints</h3>
        <p>Eli Goldratt proved it decades ago: improving a non-bottleneck doesn't improve the system. I apply this rigorously to AI implementation — we fix the constraint first, not the easy wins.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diff-card">
        <h3>I Build, Not Just Advise</h3>
        <p>I'm a full-stack developer, not just a strategist. When the diagnostic identifies the constraint, I build the solution myself — chatbots, automations, knowledge bases, custom AI systems.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="diff-card">
        <h3>Cross-Industry Pattern Recognition</h3>
        <p>Military logistics, financial derivatives operations, healthcare scheduling, pharma compliance — the bottleneck patterns repeat across industries. I've seen them all.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <MethodologySection />

  <section class="about-background section">
    <p class="section-label">Background</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">The path here</h2>

    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-label">U.S. Air Force</span>
        <p>Operations and analytics leadership in high-stakes environments. Built systems that had to work under pressure with zero margin for error.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-label">Morgan Stanley</span>
        <p>Trading floor operations — where milliseconds matter and operational efficiency directly translates to revenue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-label">Healthcare & Pharma</span>
        <p>Built a telehealth division from scratch. Navigated compliance-heavy environments where process optimization has to coexist with regulation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-label">Government</span>
        <p>Large-scale operations management in complex bureaucratic systems — finding leverage points where small changes create outsized impact.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline-item active">
        <span class="timeline-label">Unleashing Flow</span>
        <p>All of it converges here. The operational instincts, the analytical rigor, the ability to build — now applied to the most powerful tool we've ever had.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <section class="about-partner section">
    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="photo-placeholder">
        <span>Photo</span>
      </div>
      <div class="story-content">
        <p class="section-label">The Partner</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Mac Steele — new technology, new homes.</h2>
        <p>
          "I've spent my whole career selling new technology and finding it a new home.
        </p>
        <p>
          It started at a company that rethought how proxies get tabulated for large institutional investors. That's where I learned the hard part is rarely the technology itself. It's helping people see what it can do for them. From there I moved into inventory control, where we looked at the warehouse through the lens of RFID and showed companies value that was sitting on their shelves the whole time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Then came close to fifteen years at a manufacturer with over 135 years of history, taking proven technology and pushing it into industries that had never used it. The technology built on brick took us to metals, mining, steel, fly ash, and many more. Different customers, same job every time: take what the technology already does well and put it somewhere new where it creates value.
        </p>
        <p>
          That thread has never changed. Find a company's real problem, in whatever industry it lives, match it to technology that solves it, and help them pull value out of it.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's what I'm bringing to Flow."
        </p>
        <p class="partner-role">
          Mac leads business development and partnerships at Unleashing Flow — he's the one who finds the businesses with the right problems. Elliott builds the solutions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    heading="Let's find your constraint."
    subtext="Book a Throughput Diagnostic and I'll find the ONE thing limiting your business — then build the AI that fixes it."
  />
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 100px 60px 80px;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 44px);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--ivory);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .about-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--taupe);
    max-width: 580px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .story-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 280px 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .photo-placeholder {
    background: var(--ivory-dark);
    border-radius: 16px;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--taupe);
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .story-content p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
  }

  .partner-role {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--taupe);
    border-top: 1px solid #E8E0D6;
    padding-top: 16px;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  .diff-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .diff-card {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #E8E0D6;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 32px 24px;
  }

  .diff-card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--charcoal);
  }

  .diff-card p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
  }

  .timeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 640px;
  }

  .timeline-item {
    padding-left: 28px;
    border-left: 2px solid #E8E0D6;
    position: relative;
  }

  .timeline-item::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: -5px;
    top: 4px;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--taupe);
  }

  .timeline-item.active {
    border-left-color: var(--terracotta);
  }

  .timeline-item.active::before {
    background: var(--terracotta);
  }

  .timeline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--charcoal);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .timeline-item p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero {
      padding: 60px 24px 48px;
    }

    .story-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 32px;
    }

    .photo-placeholder {
      max-width: 200px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .diff-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
